# Package versions below are synced with the official ROS 2 release listed here.
# This line is the single source of truth for the pin: the release workflow reads
# it and refuses to publish if it disagrees with the release tag being built.
# To bump, pick a newer tag from https://github.com/ros2/ros2/releases, merge its
# ros2.repos versions in by URL, re-verify the patches, and update this line.
#
# ros2-release: release-lyrical-20260623
#
# DEVIATIONS from that release, all the same cause: ROS 2 is retiring vendor
# packages in favour of system libraries pulled in by rosdep. That works for a
# desktop install but not for an Android cross build, which has no system
# tinyxml2 / orocos_kdl / libyaml. These stay pinned by hand:
#   ros2/tinyxml2_vendor    0.11.3  (dropped from ros2.repos)
#   ros2/orocos_kdl_vendor  0.8.0   (dropped from ros2.repos)
#   ros2/libyaml_vendor     1.8.0   (1.8.1+ stopped vendoring libyaml)
